      "side": 0,
      "message": "Yes, the logic change is something we expected here, along with the submitted vendor hook.\n\nIf the vendor hook is attached, the vCPU would check out in a cohesive manner whenever it exits for some latest and not-yet upstreamed exit reasons, such as paravirtualization.\n\nIf the vendor hook is not attached, we found out that we don\u0027t really need the `goto` syntax to maintain the same semantics. Since the `need_userspace` variable would be set to `true`, the while loop would end, and the code snippet(`do_something()`) would be executed regardless, without explicitly using the `goto out` in the default case in the `switch`. We would align our LKML patch accordingly without the vendor hook part.\n\nas-is:\n```\nstatic long gzvm_vcpu_run(struct gzvm_vcpu *vcpu, void __user *argp)\n{\n    bool need_userspace \u003d false;\n\n    while (!need_userspace) {\n        switch (exit_reason) {\n            // snip\n            default:\n                need_userspace \u003d true;\n                goto out;\n        }\n    }\n\nout:\n    do_something();\n    return 0;\n}\n```\n\nto-be:\n```\nstatic long gzvm_vcpu_run(struct gzvm_vcpu *vcpu, void __user *argp)\n{\n    bool need_userspace \u003d false;\n\n    while (!need_userspace) {\n        switch (exit_reason) {\n            // snip\n            default:\n                need_userspace \u003d true;\n        }\n    }\n\n    do_something();\n    return 0;\n}\n```",
